on a computational pipeline to handle clustering, multiple alignment, and tree generation, including the handling of large gene families. We developed two novel non-sequence-based metrics of gene tree correctness and benchmarked a number of tree methods. The TreeBeST method from TreeFam shows the best performance in our hands. We also compared this phylogenetic approach to clustering approaches for ortholog prediction, showing a large increase in coverage using the phylogenetic approach. All data are made available in a number of formats and will be kept up to date with the Ensembl project. \u00a9 2009 by Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory Press.","authors":[{"name":"Birney E."},{"name":"Durbin R."},{"name":"Heng L."},{"name":"Severin J."},{"name":"Ureta-Vidal A."},{"name":"Vilella A.J."}],"citationCount":929,"date":"2009-02-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Research","title":"EnsemblCompara GeneTrees: Complete, duplication-aware phylogenetic trees in vertebrates"},"pmcid":"PMC2652215","pmid":"19029536","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Bioinformatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0091"},{"term":"Comparative genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0797"},{"term":"Phylogenetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3293"},{"term":"Phylogenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0194"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"Ensembl Compara","home":"https://bio.tools/Ensembl_Compara","license":"Unlicense","version":["e56","e81"],"summary":"Ensembl Compara provides cross-species resources and analyses, at both the sequence level and the gene level.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:ensembl_compara:e56/db/www.ensembl.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true,"training_materi